I have addressed both requirements and verified the fix with automated tests:

---

### 1. Shortened Highlight Pulse Duration to 2.1s (0.6x)

* **CSS Keyframes ([`style.css`](file:///d:/GitHub/[oU1TS]/events/style.css))**:
  Adjusted `.raid-card.highlighted` animation duration from `3.5s` to `2.1s` (`3.5s * 0.6 = 2.1s`):
  ```css
  .raid-card.highlighted {
      animation: highlightPulse 2.1s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) forwards;
      z-index: 10;
      border-color: var(--accent) !important;
  }
  ```
* **Timer Buffer ([`app.js`](file:///d:/GitHub/[oU1TS]/events/app.js))**:
  Adjusted JavaScript fallback timer `activeHighlightTimeout` from `3600ms` down to `2200ms` (2.1s animation + 100ms safety buffer).

---

### 2. Manual Expansion Toggle Immediately Stops Highlight Animation

* Implemented `stopHighlightAnimation(card)` in [`app.js`](file:///d:/GitHub/[oU1TS]/events/app.js):
  ```javascript
  function stopHighlightAnimation(card) {
      if (!card) return;
      card.classList.remove('highlighted');
      if (activeHighlightTimeout) {
          clearTimeout(activeHighlightTimeout);
          activeHighlightTimeout = null;
      }
      if (pendingReRender) {
          const fn = pendingReRender;
          pendingReRender = null;
          fn();
      }
  }
  ```
* Attached to the card's native `<details>` `'toggle'` event, the `<summary>` click handler, and the selectable card title click handler so that any manual user interaction (collapse or expand) **instantly removes `.highlighted` and stops the animation**.
* Added an `isProgrammaticScrollOpening` guard to ensure the initial automatic opening upon URL navigation doesn't prematurely cancel the glow before it starts.

---

### 3. Eliminated State Reversion on Animation End

* **Why it occurred**:
  When the highlight pulse ended, queued background updates from Supabase invoked `renderRaids()`. In `renderRaids()`, the check:
  `const isTargetedRaid = ... || (window.location.hash === '#raid-22'); if (openCardIds.has(card.id) || isTargetedRaid) card.open = true;`
  evaluated to `true` because `window.location.hash` was still `#raid-22`. This caused the card to be **forcibly popped open again** even if you had manually retracted it!
* **The Fix**:
  Added a `hasRenderedBefore` check in `renderRaids()`:
  ```javascript
  const hasRenderedBefore = raidsContainer.querySelector('.parent-raid-card') !== null;
  ...
  if (hasRenderedBefore) {
      card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id);
  } else {
      const isTargetedRaid = (pendingRaidScroll === raid.Raid_Num) ||
          (window.location.hash === `#raid-${raid.Raid_Num}`);
      card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id) || isTargetedRaid;
  }
  ```
  Once cards have rendered in the DOM, background updates strictly respect `openCardIds.has(card.id)`—ensuring that if you manually collapsed a card, it **never** gets reverted back to open.

